    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Ryan are pleased to present 15 Ballydaheen East, Mallow to the market for sale. This two-bedroom mid-terrace property occupies a convenient location within Mallow town, just a short walk from a wide range of amenities and services.\n\nExtending to C. 50 sqm over two floors, the property comprises a compact residential layout with two bedrooms and one bathroom. The house is in need of complete renovation works throughout, presenting an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to modernise and redesign the property to their own taste and requirements.\n\nTo the rear is a private garden, offering valuable outdoor space and further scope to enhance the property.\n\nThe location is a particular advantage, with Mallow town centre and its excellent selection of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, recreational facilities and transport links all within easy reach.\n\nThe property is currently vacant and is being sold chain free, allowing for a straightforward sale process. With its central location and considerable potential, 15 Ballydaheen East is ideally suited to homeowners, investors or purchasers seeking a renovation project in Mallow.\n\nViewing is strictly by appointment with sole selling agents DNG Ryan.\n\nKEY FEATURES:\n2 bed, 1 bath\nMid terrace property\nExpands to C. 50sqm\nMains sewage\nMains water\nLocated in Mallow town\nGarden to the rear\nIn need of complete renovation throughout\nHuge potential \n\nThese particulars have been prepared by DNG John Ryan and whilst every care has been taken to ensure that these are accurate and correct, we are not responsible for any errors, omissions, inaccuracies, if the property is let, sold or withdrawn from sale or if it is not suitable for your purpose. These particulars are for information only and are given under the strict understanding that they do not form part of any contract. Neither whole nor any part of this document or any reference thereto may be included in any public document, circular or statement nor published without the written consent of DNG John Ryan. PSL: 003615"
      },
